00:01:48.310 --> 00:01:54.360
Fluffy, fluffy, fluffiness, so sweetly it melts.

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:59.700
shiawase wo ageru yo yumeiro no pâtishièeru<i>!!</i>

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:59.700
I'll give happiness to you, the dream-coloured Pâtissière<i>!!</i>

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:04.240
ichigo furejie & furanbowaazu, hapihapi makaron, fun fun

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:04.240
Strawberry Fraisier & Framboise, happy happy Macaron, fun, fun

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:06.410
yume ni eeru<i>!</i>

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:06.410
Get them in our dreams<i>!</i>

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:10.920
Presented by Wasurenai-subs

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:18.980
We've meet again! Yumeiro Pâtissière is brought to you by Konami and these other sponsors.

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:29.190
and are each heading to a three-star pâtisserie for some practical training for three days!

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:38.250
Ichigo, you can do it!

00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:39.390
What are you doing?

00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:40.800
Get on up here already!

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:43.240
You damned devil...

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:44.930
Ichigo, fight!

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:53.510
Is this it?

00:02:55.350 --> 00:02:56.470
It seems...

00:02:56.850 --> 00:03:00.790
Yeah... For a three-star pâtisserie it's...

00:03:00.790 --> 00:03:01.830
...kinda shabby.

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:08.520
recipe 43

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:08.520
Underneath the Orange Tree

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:12.570
Ah, here it is.

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:15.850
What a splendid hotel!

00:03:15.850 --> 00:03:19.080
So pâtisserie Noir is in this hotel's lounge?

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:22.080
The shop might be shabby but the sweets are top-notch!

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:23.420
Éclairs...

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:25.290
Tarte aux poires...

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:27.000
Bon bon chocolats...

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:28.840
Mousse aux framboises!

00:03:30.340 --> 00:03:33.780
Amano, did you forget why we came here?

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:36.180
Does your gluttony know no bounds?

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:39.180
But they look so delicious...

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:41.100
Don't you think the selection's kind of sparse?

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:42.820
A three-star pâtisserie should have more...

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:44.840
Yeah...

00:03:45.270 --> 00:03:47.980
But, look at all the bread!

00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:51.190
Baguettes that are crispy on the outside, and fluffy on the inside!

00:03:51.190 --> 00:03:53.320
Croissants chock full of butter!

00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:56.530
Even quiches made with fresh milk and vegetables!

00:03:57.300 --> 00:03:59.370
They all look so delicious!

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:02.200
Do you even care as long as it is edible?

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:03.250
Hey!

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:11.900
Bonjour, Monsieur...

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:12.510
Monsieur...

00:04:12.510 --> 00:04:15.180
I am the owner of the shop, Robert Blanc.

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:23.330
Oh, just great...

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:25.190
Can she handle this?

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:29.450
Which one is a parisian?

00:04:29.450 --> 00:04:31.770
I don't really know bread names too well...

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:32.990
Amano!

00:04:32.990 --> 00:04:34.750
Hurry up!

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:36.370
The customer is waiting!

00:04:36.370 --> 00:04:38.250
I know that!

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:45.710
Rather than a parisian, why don't you try one of these pain aux raisins?

00:04:45.710 --> 00:04:49.270
Raisins sweetened underneath the sun's rays,

00:04:49.270 --> 00:04:54.260
and milk from cows raised on a laid-back farm, all wrapped into a danish!

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:58.090
You'll feel all Bourgogne in no time!

00:05:00.510 --> 00:05:02.350
Amano...

00:05:00.510 --> 00:05:02.350
Ichigo...

00:05:02.350 --> 00:05:04.010
Pardon, Madame.

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:06.700
Blanc-san...

00:05:08.290 --> 00:05:10.110
Merci, Madame.

00:05:10.110 --> 00:05:11.730
Au revoir...

00:05:20.700 --> 00:05:22.890
I'm sorry, Monsieur Blanc!

00:05:24.250 --> 00:05:27.120
I'll have you two do something more appropriate.

00:05:31.410 --> 00:05:34.190
Look at all these...

00:05:34.190 --> 00:05:36.300
Dried fruits and different types of rums?

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:39.300
Over here they are preserved in sugar and jams!

00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:44.250
This lemon jam is so invigorating!

00:05:44.250 --> 00:05:45.520
We don't have time to be goofing off!

00:05:45.830 --> 00:05:48.200
Hurry and help carry the wheat flour!

00:05:48.510 --> 00:05:49.800
Oh, right...

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:52.190
Sheesh...

00:05:52.190 --> 00:05:53.650
This is your fault, Amano.

00:05:53.650 --> 00:05:55.270
You're why we're stuck helping in the storehouse.

00:05:55.270 --> 00:05:56.500
Sorry.

00:05:56.500 --> 00:05:58.540
But isn't it kind of fun?

00:05:58.540 --> 00:06:00.250
There're all these ingredients!

00:06:00.970 --> 00:06:04.320
I'm not sure if you look on the bright side or just ain't too bright.

00:06:04.320 --> 00:06:06.100
I vote for the latter.

00:06:09.350 --> 00:06:10.250
Anyway...

00:06:11.060 --> 00:06:12.920
Anyway, we've got to get into the kitchen.

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:15.190
Otherwise there's no point to us coming here for practicals.

00:06:16.150 --> 00:06:19.150
I wonder how Andou-kun and Hanabusa-kun are doing?

00:06:19.150 --> 00:06:21.170
I'm sure they're in the same boat as us.

00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:26.130
Andou!

00:06:26.130 --> 00:06:28.060
Caramel, where have you been?

00:06:28.060 --> 00:06:30.100
It's amazing!

00:06:30.100 --> 00:06:34.110
There's a giant pool, and a high-class restaurant!

00:06:34.110 --> 00:06:37.600
And of course the sweets here are amazing too!

00:06:38.170 --> 00:06:40.170
I guess it's not a four-star hotel for nothing.

00:06:40.170 --> 00:06:42.780
The kitchen is huge, too.

00:06:42.780 --> 00:06:46.620
That's because all the sweets for this hotel are made here.

00:06:46.620 --> 00:06:49.680
Oh, so that's how Japanese sweets are made?

00:06:50.150 --> 00:06:51.790
Yes, it is!

00:06:51.790 --> 00:06:54.380
I look forward to the tasting tonight.

00:06:57.200 --> 00:06:59.060
And you are making Sweets Crafts?

00:06:59.060 --> 00:06:59.820
Yes.

00:07:01.700 --> 00:07:03.360
That's not bad at all.

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:04.740
Ah, Chef...

00:07:05.460 --> 00:07:08.840
We have a request from the guests in the suite...

00:07:09.520 --> 00:07:12.850
This rose, for your beauty...

00:07:12.850 --> 00:07:13.560
Oh, my...

00:07:18.210 --> 00:07:20.780
All cleaned up!

00:07:25.400 --> 00:07:26.240
Huh?

00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:28.080
W-What?

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:34.130
Amano, where are you going?

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:36.130
Hey!

00:07:39.080 --> 00:07:41.050
What a reposeful little garden!

00:07:44.500 --> 00:07:46.720
So this is what it was!

00:07:47.950 --> 00:07:49.380
What a great smell!

00:07:49.380 --> 00:07:54.110
Watched over by the sun, you sucked up this fresh air and water,

00:07:54.110 --> 00:07:56.730
and got more and more delicious, didn't you?

00:07:56.730 --> 00:08:00.220
Amano! Don't go picking them without permission!

00:08:00.220 --> 00:08:02.860
I wasn't gonna...

00:08:03.690 --> 00:08:07.740
But maybe, just maybe, the oranges are saying "eat me!" and will fall for me!

00:08:09.400 --> 00:08:10.040
Idiot...

00:08:10.040 --> 00:08:11.670
I think the votes are in.

00:08:26.450 --> 00:08:27.790
Hey, Amano!

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:35.480
Get in the kitchen.

00:08:38.750 --> 00:08:39.940
All right!

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:45.850
We're in the kitchen, but all we're doing is cleaning up.

00:08:45.850 --> 00:08:47.700
He didn't teach us a thing.

00:08:47.700 --> 00:08:50.860
Techniques aren't things you are taught; they're things you steal!

00:08:50.860 --> 00:08:52.850
So watch closely and remember.

00:08:52.850 --> 00:08:53.960
Oh, right...

00:09:03.130 --> 00:09:04.670
Tarte aux noix!

00:09:06.040 --> 00:09:07.040
I'll wash it!

00:09:11.190 --> 00:09:12.450
It's wiped clean!

00:09:12.450 --> 00:09:14.200
He used it all...

00:09:14.200 --> 00:09:16.350
But we can still lick the bowl!

00:09:16.350 --> 00:09:17.510
Don't even think about it!

00:09:17.510 --> 00:09:19.250
That's so unrefined!

00:09:19.250 --> 00:09:20.550
Chocolat!

00:09:20.550 --> 00:09:22.260
Let me lick it!

00:09:22.810 --> 00:09:24.580
Eggs, sugar...

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:27.200
And wheat flour. Those are obvious.

00:09:27.550 --> 00:09:32.980
Then, there's almond powder, chocolate, and cheese in it?

00:09:34.400 --> 00:09:35.850
What do you think, Kashino?

00:09:38.200 --> 00:09:40.420
Well, I don't really...

00:09:40.420 --> 00:09:42.610
I think it's cheese, anyway.

00:09:45.900 --> 00:09:48.040
What's the matter, Kashino?

00:09:48.040 --> 00:09:51.800
Oh, I was just thinking how good a nose you have, Amano...

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:56.430
But unless I taste it, I can't be sure.

00:10:10.120 --> 00:10:13.750
The balance between the cassis purée and the liqueur is sublime!

00:10:13.750 --> 00:10:18.580
He used heavy cream, but it's not heavy, in fact it turned out light!

00:10:24.140 --> 00:10:26.340
Those bon bon chocolats, are they abricot?

00:10:28.090 --> 00:10:30.960
He uses dried apricots, I see.

00:10:30.960 --> 00:10:32.650
But they're so fresh!

00:10:32.650 --> 00:10:34.810
They taste almost like they're freshly picked.

00:10:35.670 --> 00:10:37.150
Merci, Madame.

00:10:41.420 --> 00:10:43.180
This sponge is so fluffy!

00:10:43.180 --> 00:10:45.380
The texture is extremely fine...

00:10:50.290 --> 00:10:52.110
These are the ingredients for dinner?

00:10:52.110 --> 00:10:54.290
He said to make it with what was in the refrigerator.

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:55.870
Just this?

00:10:57.200 --> 00:11:02.380
You can't become a first-rate pâtissier unless you can cook everything, not just sweets.

00:11:04.060 --> 00:11:05.210
Wow!

00:11:06.480 --> 00:11:08.480
This is our dinner?

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:10.360
There's a lobster and moules in it...

00:11:10.760 --> 00:11:12.900
This is way too amazing.

00:11:12.900 --> 00:11:15.720
There's a big party at the hotel today, see.

00:11:16.060 --> 00:11:18.430
We made it using those ingredients.

00:11:18.900 --> 00:11:20.350
Even so...

00:11:20.350 --> 00:11:22.140
...it's just too much...

00:11:22.940 --> 00:11:25.000
Wow, looks delicious!

00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:27.150
I love this kind of food.

00:11:27.150 --> 00:11:28.350
Like pot-au-feu...

00:11:28.350 --> 00:11:30.690
Then learn how to make it yourself!

00:11:31.550 --> 00:11:32.410
You have a point.

00:11:43.950 --> 00:11:45.110
Blanc-san...

00:11:50.510 --> 00:11:53.220
Umm, dinner is ready.

00:12:13.700 --> 00:12:15.550
He nodded!

00:12:15.550 --> 00:12:17.680
Yeah! I think that means he likes it!

00:12:18.930 --> 00:12:22.850
Blanc-san, have you always run this shop by yourself?

00:12:23.210 --> 00:12:23.920
No.

00:12:28.370 --> 00:12:29.800
Back then...

00:12:32.270 --> 00:12:34.250
This was delicious!

00:12:35.900 --> 00:12:37.610
This is what you made earlier today?

00:12:37.610 --> 00:12:39.880
Tarte aux noix.

00:12:39.880 --> 00:12:40.930
Are you sure?

00:12:41.930 --> 00:12:44.140
Itadakimasu!

00:12:47.110 --> 00:12:49.290
The crust of this tart is really flaky!

00:12:49.290 --> 00:12:52.170
There's plenty of butter but it's not too heavy!

00:12:52.170 --> 00:12:53.980
An appareil with nuts.

00:12:53.980 --> 00:12:57.040
And just like you said, there's cheese in it.

00:12:57.040 --> 00:12:57.700
I'm sure of it.

00:12:58.640 --> 00:13:01.370
I'm so happy we got to come here for training...

00:13:02.820 --> 00:13:04.700
It's so high class!

00:13:04.700 --> 00:13:06.200
Could this be...

00:13:06.200 --> 00:13:09.670
A suite decked out for romance?

00:13:11.250 --> 00:13:13.870
Two guys in a suite?

00:13:13.870 --> 00:13:15.880
This is kind of... ew.

00:13:20.310 --> 00:13:22.600
Hey, this is...

00:13:22.600 --> 00:13:23.890
Uh, oh...

00:13:35.270 --> 00:13:37.630
There's only one bed!

00:13:37.630 --> 00:13:39.000
What if you rock-paper-scissors for it?

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:40.310
The winner gets the bed.

00:13:41.120 --> 00:13:43.830
I can sleep on half of it.

00:13:43.830 --> 00:13:45.240
Half and half...

00:13:48.270 --> 00:13:50.070
Do you even... Ichigo?

00:13:50.650 --> 00:13:52.040
'Night.

00:13:53.140 --> 00:13:55.050
Hey, don't just go to sleep!

00:13:56.390 --> 00:13:58.410
Hey, wake up!

00:13:58.410 --> 00:13:59.310
Wake up, Amano!

00:13:59.310 --> 00:14:00.700
I'll help!

00:14:00.700 --> 00:14:02.830
Ichigo, wake up!

00:14:02.830 --> 00:14:04.000
Ichigo!

00:14:14.440 --> 00:14:16.400
How is this half and half?

00:14:17.830 --> 00:14:19.740
Kashino...

00:14:25.160 --> 00:14:26.450
What is it?

00:14:29.830 --> 00:14:33.480
Hey, pick the orange...

00:14:33.480 --> 00:14:35.550
The orange in the garden...

00:14:35.880 --> 00:14:37.140
I wanna eat it.

00:14:47.800 --> 00:14:49.820
It's morning already?

00:14:54.360 --> 00:14:56.050
What the heck?!

00:14:56.050 --> 00:14:58.240
Amano, how long do you plan to stay in bed?

00:14:58.240 --> 00:15:00.570
Like I have a choice?

00:15:02.570 --> 00:15:05.830
Wow! The courtyard's turned into a market!

00:15:05.830 --> 00:15:08.000
And look at all the fresh produce!

00:15:08.350 --> 00:15:11.450
You two split up and help me buy these things.

00:15:11.450 --> 00:15:12.210
Right!

00:15:13.610 --> 00:15:17.210
Cherries, grapes, and then apricots.

00:15:18.050 --> 00:15:21.050
Apples, pears, and lemons?

00:15:21.050 --> 00:15:22.630
That, that!

00:15:28.270 --> 00:15:29.390
No, no, no, no!

00:15:29.390 --> 00:15:31.440
Put these in! These!

00:15:33.400 --> 00:15:34.950
It's pretty heavy.

00:15:38.570 --> 00:15:39.630
She...

00:15:39.970 --> 00:15:40.780
Kashino?

00:15:41.560 --> 00:15:44.110
Oranges weren't on the shopping list, right?

00:15:44.520 --> 00:15:50.120
After all, the oranges from the tree in Blanc-san's yard have got to be way yummier.

00:15:50.120 --> 00:15:51.370
I was just looking at them!

00:15:51.370 --> 00:15:53.480
Yeah, I totally understand...

00:15:53.480 --> 00:15:55.710
Makes you wanna eat 'em, right?

00:15:56.670 --> 00:16:00.390
I wonder what he'll make with all these cherries?

00:16:01.380 --> 00:16:06.430
I'll preserve them in sugar and dry them, or make them into a jam.

00:16:06.430 --> 00:16:08.430
In the storehouse...

00:16:08.430 --> 00:16:13.230
Wait, you made all those dried fruits and jams by yourself?

00:16:13.230 --> 00:16:14.320
Yes.

00:16:14.320 --> 00:16:15.670
That would explain...

00:16:15.670 --> 00:16:20.160
The smell and flavour of the ones we use at school are totally different...

00:16:20.160 --> 00:16:22.820
When you're done, you can eat this.

00:16:23.650 --> 00:16:25.010
An orange from the garden!

00:16:25.010 --> 00:16:25.780
Yay!

00:16:25.780 --> 00:16:28.860
It's 'cause you were drooling over it, Ichigo.

00:16:28.860 --> 00:16:30.160
But something is weird.

00:16:30.160 --> 00:16:30.830
What?

00:16:31.180 --> 00:16:33.830
He has such wonderful oranges in his garden,

00:16:33.830 --> 00:16:37.430
but it's strange that none of the sweets he makes use oranges.

00:16:37.750 --> 00:16:39.840
Now that you mention it...

00:16:39.840 --> 00:16:42.690
Anyway, hurry and eat it!

00:16:42.690 --> 00:16:43.920
That's right!

00:16:43.920 --> 00:16:45.760
You finally got it, so do it!

00:16:45.760 --> 00:16:46.430
No!

00:16:47.640 --> 00:16:50.940
It'd be such a waste to eat it!

00:16:52.280 --> 00:16:54.350
Do whatever you want...

00:17:25.430 --> 00:17:27.840
The training will be over tomorrow, right?

00:17:27.840 --> 00:17:28.600
Yeah.

00:17:29.050 --> 00:17:32.210
And thanks to you, it was a heck of a lot of trouble.

00:17:33.950 --> 00:17:34.910
Sorry.

00:17:36.850 --> 00:17:42.050
Blanc-san looked lonely when he stared at this orange tree.

00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:44.980
Yeah?

00:17:48.370 --> 00:17:52.870
Making sweets as a thank you gift for a three-star pâtisserie chef?

00:17:52.870 --> 00:17:55.340
You seriously know no fear.

00:17:55.340 --> 00:17:56.040
What?

00:17:56.040 --> 00:17:58.780
Weren't you thinking the same thing, Kashino?

00:17:59.300 --> 00:18:00.240
Well...

00:18:00.240 --> 00:18:02.670
It was a pretty good idea. For Ichigo, that is.

00:18:02.670 --> 00:18:04.090
Yeah!

00:18:04.090 --> 00:18:08.510
If you and Ichigo want to give it your best, you've got to make sweets!

00:18:38.410 --> 00:18:40.750
Thank you for allowing us to train here.

00:18:41.190 --> 00:18:44.390
In return, we've made a tarte à l'orange together for you.

00:18:44.750 --> 00:18:46.840
We hope it's to your liking...

00:18:50.510 --> 00:18:51.890
I see.

00:18:51.890 --> 00:18:53.600
Then, I will eat it.

00:19:04.000 --> 00:19:07.980
Robert, it seems like we've got another great crop of oranges this year!

00:19:18.600 --> 00:19:21.590
Michelle... My wife.

00:19:21.590 --> 00:19:23.840
This is her tarte à l'orange.

00:19:24.880 --> 00:19:29.680
The chocolate ganache, the orange compote...

00:19:30.110 --> 00:19:34.480
This is, without a doubt, my late wife's tarte à l'orange.

00:19:35.640 --> 00:19:36.850
Then...

00:19:36.850 --> 00:19:40.570
You said we should use the orange, Amano...

00:19:40.570 --> 00:19:43.010
And I suggested the chocolate sauce...

00:19:43.010 --> 00:19:43.850
Then...

00:19:44.190 --> 00:19:49.200
The orange tart that resulted from Kashino and Ichigo giving their best was,

00:19:49.200 --> 00:19:54.370
shockingly, the same flavour as a tart in his memories.

00:19:55.750 --> 00:19:58.290
That character is totally inappropriate!

00:19:59.900 --> 00:20:04.540
My wife specialized in sweets that used oranges.

00:20:04.540 --> 00:20:05.510
But...

00:20:13.850 --> 00:20:19.960
Ever since that day, orange sweets have disappeared from pâtisserie Blanc.

00:20:24.060 --> 00:20:24.940
